```css
.box {
  width: 200px;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 5px solid #334155;
  margin: 16px;
}

/* common global fix */
*, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
```

| box-sizing | width: 200px means | Outer border-box width |
|---|---|---|
| content-box (default). | content only. | 250px. |
| border-box. | content + padding + border. | 200px (content shrinks to 150px). |

Margin (16px each side) is **never** included in either — it's space around the box.

